# WASM_SEC — emit_n ovf latch and emit-wasm check gate

File: openOODA/audit/wasm_sec.oot
SEC on the WASM lane. Own this note only. Did not edit product .oo or .c.

Logline: emit_n does not clear the overflow latch at entry, and emit-wasm still runs check before emit.
Setup: Static read of ooda/runtime/chs_rt_wasm_print.c and ooda/oodac/main.oo.
Beats:
  1. State ovf-not-cleared and check-before-emit.
  2. Quote emit_n entry and first ovf use.
  3. Quote the only ovf = 0 site (not emit_n).
  4. Quote the emit-wasm arm order.

## 0. Verdict

ovf-not-cleared: yes
check-before-emit: yes

No CRIT. No HIGH. No product patch. Did not rebuild oodac.

## 1. emit_n does not assign oo_wasm_ovf = 0 at entry

File: ooda/runtime/chs_rt_wasm_print.c

Entry (exact):

  static void oo_wasm_emit_n(unsigned int n) {
    static unsigned char pay[24000], mod[28000];
    unsigned int i, psz, mlen, nlen, main_i = 0, base = 0;
    const char *nm;
    static const unsigned char hv[8] = {0x00, 0x61, 0x73, 0x6d,
                                        0x01, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00};

Those are print.c lines 114-119. Next statements clamp n, bind
a pending print, and scan names. None assign oo_wasm_ovf.

First ovf use in emit_n (print.c 144-147, a read):

  if (oo_wasm_ovf) {
    oo_wasm_emit_tiny();
    return;
  }

Later read (print.c 233-236) is the same fail-closed return.
emit_n never writes oo_wasm_ovf.

The only `oo_wasm_ovf = 0` in the two runtime wasm C files is
print.c 83-85 inside oo_wasm_emit_print_body, not at emit_n entry:

  int saveo = oo_wasm_ovf;
  oo_wasm_lim = 64u;
  oo_wasm_ovf = 0;

chs_rt_wasm.c only assigns oo_wasm_ovf = 1 on leb/raw/u8 overflow.

## 2. emit-wasm still calls run_check_core first

File: ooda/oodac/main.oo lines 228-232 (exact):

    if cmd == "emit-wasm" {
        let src: String = load_source_with_imports(fs, path);
        run_check_core(sys, src);
        wasm_emit_stream(src);
        return;
    }

Order: load, run_check_core, wasm_emit_stream. Check is line 230.
Emit is line 231. wasm_emit_stream is not reached if check exits.

## 3. Isolation

Wrote only openOODA/audit/wasm_sec.oot.
Did not edit oodac, runtime, fixtures, or smokes.
Did not clear ovf. Did not rebuild oodac.

Status: PASS. Both proofs hold on disk.
